<title>MEXICO: Two Mexican crude ports closed due to cold front.</title>
<headline>Two Mexican crude ports closed due to cold front.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Mexican crude ports along the Gulf of Mexico were shut on Thursday as a new cold front hit the region, port authorities said on Friday.</p>
<p>Pajaritos in Veracruz was reported shut at 1330 local/1930 GMT, while Dos Bocas in Tabasco was closed at 1600 local/2200 GMT, port officials said.</p>
<p>At Pajaritos winds were reportedly at 20 to 25 km per hour with waves four to five feet high and weather conditions were improving. Wind s were a steady 45 km per hour with waves nine to 12 feet high at Dos Bocas, officials said.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
